[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2503647743","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99728#issuecomment-2503647743","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99728","id":2503647743,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VOqH_","user":{"login":"Faless","id":1687918,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2ODc5MTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1687918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless","html_url":"https://github.com/Faless","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-27T11:36:29Z","updated_at":"2024-11-27T11:50:30Z","body":"Some screenshots from my tests on Linux.\n\nSystem: Debian GNU/Linux 12 (bookworm), Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 980 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6603) - Intel® Core™ i7-7700K × 8\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0fe1d3cf-aaa9-4f6a-9bb6-d817ca14a1a5)\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/99cf9c63-61ef-4737-b978-062ab1f3d17d)\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8782e60e-54d9-4adc-9c29-83c621782bc3)\n\nSo, at least on Linux, there doesn't seem to be any specific issues with the sleep functions and frame pacing, and the (small) fluctuations happens in any case, even with unlimited max_fps and the loop is just regulated by vsync (i.e. we add no frame delay).\n\nAm I missing something?","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2503647743/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2504786222","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99728#issuecomment-2504786222","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99728","id":2504786222,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VTAEu","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-27T21:20:28Z","updated_at":"2024-11-27T21:20:28Z","body":"> Am I missing something?\n\nI think its best to treat this as a Windows issue. We know that frame pacing is bad on Windows due to the `Sleep` function being inaccurate. Your screenshots show that Linux also isn't able to achieve a stable frame rate, but the fluctuations are much smaller and the root cause likely isn't from the OS sleep function. \n\nWe really shouldn't be blocking fixing this just because Linux handles sleep better than Windows though.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2504786222/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2504807585","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99728#issuecomment-2504807585","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99728","id":2504807585,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VTFSh","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-27T21:38:10Z","updated_at":"2024-11-27T21:48:24Z","body":"On my MacBook Pro M3 Max (adaptative 120fps screen): \n> Godot v4.4.dev (f128f383e) - macOS 15.1.1 - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M3 Max (Apple9) - Apple M3 Max (16 threads)\n\n| Renderer | Unlimited | 60fps |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| Metal | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/94799085-d16b-4ef8-bc91-85f9f9e36fcf) | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b716ef79-0672-4e16-b906-6b0b1fcf1979) |\n| MoltenVK | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e3c6fddd-6251-45b6-b58a-1c4e125a7468) | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/933a82fc-1518-48e3-9f4e-350f1e4cf1c2) |\n| OpenGL | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/df33d5d1-bbaf-41c6-9bed-4bacb095db11) | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4e290556-4639-4f43-83d6-94ac740bc129) | \n\nFullscreen seems to be the same results.\n\n@Calinou As the resolution/graph is inconsistent, can you add a label that could sum up the variation or something like that? Like the median difference in values.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2504807585/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2504842104","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99728#issuecomment-2504842104","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99728","id":2504842104,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VTNt4","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organiza